; patch.hl - the OUT stream of the original patch.asm
; The .asm original demonstrates self-modifying code: it rewrites its
; own ADD instruction to display 7 then 9 forever. The language does
; not expose code addresses (an accidental self-write is exactly the
; "dumb thing" it refuses), so this produces the same display by
; ordinary means. Display: 7, 9, 9, 9, ...
var y = 9
out 7
while 1:
    out y
